 "validation": {
  "file_check": "Raw files written in the AncestryDNA, 23andMe, MyHeritage, FamilyTreeDNA, Living DNA and VCF layouts (including a GRCh38 VCF) are read back with every genotype exact.",
  "pca": "Genomes reduced to about 252,881 SNPs (a genotyping chip's worth) land a median 0.29% of the map's width from where the same genomes land with all 1.15 million SNPs (186 placements of 93 held-out genomes).",
  "neanderthal": "On 93 held-out genomes reduced to chip size, the 95% interval contained the estimate from all 1.15 million SNPs in 100% of cases.",
  "ancient_ancestry": "Athanor's qpAdm reproduces ADMIXTOOLS qpAdm [0.524, 0.282, 0.195] with [0.524, 0.282, 0.194] on a well-powered simulation: every weight agrees to within 0.0006 and every standard error to within 0.0003, and both recover the simulated proportions [0.5, 0.3, 0.2] to within 0.024. On 1 of 1 held-out present-day population targets, Athanor's qpAdm agrees with ADMIXTOOLS qpAdm (v8.0.2) to within two standard errors (largest difference 0.047).",
  "y_haplogroup": "On 600 ancient men with published Y haplogroups, Athanor's call from the 1240K Y-chromosome SNPs was on the same lineage in 98% and identical in 34%.",
  "mt_haplogroup": "On 1500 ancient mitogenomes with published haplogroups, Athanor's call was on the same lineage in 98% and identical in 83%; from only 1,500 positions, of the kind a genotyping chip reads, on the same lineage in 94%.",
  "continental_ancestry": "On 16 simulated genomes mixing two or three continents, built from the chromosomes of reference people left out of the panels whose own ancestry is unambiguous, the proportions were within 2.6 percentage points on average (7.2 at worst); the 95% intervals, which reflect statistical noise only, contained the true value 61% of the time. On genomes built from any reference people, including members of mixed groups, results matched the sources' own compositions within 1.7 points on average. Reference people left out of their panel are assigned on average at least 58% to their own continent; the rest mostly reflects real shared ancestry between neighbouring regions, which is why each region's typical profile is shown. ADMIXTURE's projection mode gives the same proportions to within 0.004.",
